A wet run over an artifact carrying no `metrics_*` key stamps all six of them and reports `written`
true. The `expected/` section is the real assertion — stdout's flag says a write happened, not that
the right numbers landed — and it also pins that the pre-existing keys, their order, and the body
survive the round trip.

Arithmetic, two seeded sessions:
  s-alpha — one turn, 10:00:00 → 10:08:00 = 480s; tokens input 100, output 20, cache creation 300,
    cache read 50; model claude-fx-sonnet.
  s-beta  — one turn, 11:00:00 → 11:03:00 = 180s; tokens input 7, output 3, no cache fields = 0;
    model claude-fx-opus.
  totals  — (480 + 180) / 60 = 11 minutes; input 107, output 23, cache creation 300, cache read 50;
    models sorted, so opus precedes sonnet.
Per-session minutes are 8 and 3, which sum to the same 11 here only by luck — the total is rounded
from summed seconds, never from summed minutes.

